---
description: Use StatsHawk MCP tools for real sports statistics instead of estimating from training data.
alwaysApply: false
---

When the user asks for scores, standings, box scores, rosters, game logs,
injuries, player props, hit rates, matchups, or betting lines, use the
StatsHawk MCP tools. Do not invent numbers from memory.

- Resolve players with `search_player` before any person-keyed call.
- Resolve games with `search_games` (or `get_mlb_matchups` for MLB slates)
  before box scores, play-by-play, or odds.
- Every number must come from a tool result. If a stat is missing, say so.
- Do not call StatsHawk live or real-time. It is ingested data, current
  through a date; lag is typically minutes to about a day by feed.
- State the season, the through-date, and the games counted. Odds are
  pregame, not in-play.
